 ation and data-driven modeling for dynamical systems and control. Charact
 eristic themes include nonlinear identification\, model reduction\, ident
 ification software and benchmarks\, learning across systems\, and dynamic
  networks. Application tracks remain grounded in identifying or learning 
 dynamical models\, rather than becoming general-purpose domain conference
 s.\nAdditional topics: Nonlinear Dynamics & Chaos\, Complex Systems & Net
 work Science\nScope sources (2027): https://conferences.ifac-control.org/
 sysid2027/participate/\nScope last checked: 2026-10-07
